  "type": "singleCorrect",
  "level": 2,
  "question": {
    "text": "Pressure-volume $(p V)$ work done by an ideal gaseous system at constant volume is (where $E$ is internal energy of the system)",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "N0g5J",
      "text": "$-\\Delta p / p$",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "kWjyJ",
      "text": "zero",
      "isCorrect": true,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "EdtYF",
      "text": "$-V \\Delta p$",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "t8iWx",
      "text": "$-\\Delta E$",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "From first law of thermodynamics\r\n$$\r\n\\Delta E=q+W\r\n$$\r\nwhere, work do net $(W)=p \\Delta V$\r\n$$\r\n\\begin{array}{l}\r\n=p \\times \\Delta V \\\\\r\n=0\r\n\\end{array} \\quad(\\because \\Delta V=0)\r\n$$",
    "image": null
  },
